Triumph Adler Alphatronic P2, ITT 3030, SKS KISS

(NOTE: the dissected disk image is not strictly 
necessary here, with some cpmtools version it is
possible to edit directly an IMD disk image).

This is sample procedure to use CPMTOOLS to create 
a bootable disk image with your own files
(an MS-DOS emulator is required to run bin2imd)

    copy /B ta-p2_bios.raw+ta-p2_body.raw test.raw /y
    \cpmtools\cpmcp -f tap2 test.raw %1 0:
    msdos bin2imd test.raw test.imd cpm22.b2i

--------------------------------

CPMTOOLS DISKDEFS:

# Triumph-Adler P2
# (Same geometry of NEC PC-6001/6601)

diskdef tap2
  seclen 256
  tracks 40
  sectrk 16
  blocksize 1024
  maxdir 64
  skew 0
  boottrk 2
  os 2.2
end


--------------------------------

CPM22.B2I

0  N=40  DM=5  SS=256 SM=1-16 /1

--------------------------------
